    <h3>Streaks and Clustering</h3>
    <p>Several composers have won in back-to-back years. Franz Waxman won consecutively in 1950–1951 (<em>Sunset Boulevard</em>, <em>A Place in the Sun</em>). Gustavo Santaolalla repeated in 2005–2006 (<em>Brokeback Mountain</em>, <em>Babel</em>). Most dramatically, Ludwig Göransson won in 2023 and 2024 — both for <em>Oppenheimer</em> — and then again in 2026, making him the only composer in this dataset to win three times within a four-year window.</p>

    <p>The longest gap between wins belongs to <strong>Hans Zimmer</strong>: 27 years elapsed between his first win for <em>The Lion King</em> (1994) and his second for <em>Dune</em> (2021). John Barry's gap of 17 years (1968 to 1985) and Maurice Jarre's 19-year gap (1965 to 1984) are the next most notable.</p>

